==Trivia==
*This event is based on [[wikipedia:Hinamatsuri Hinamatsuri/Girls' Day|Hinamatsuri]], a Japanese holiday held on March 3rd in which ornamental dolls, called ''hina-ningyō'' (雛人形), are displayed on a tiered stand known as a ''hinadan'' (雛壇).
*''Hinadan'' may also refer to tiered seats/platforms for kabuki musicians or ministers in the National Diet, similar to the [[Bears Be Bare]]' bleachers.

